\fs29\fsmilli14857 \cf2 \cb3 4. Analysis \'97 what this actually says\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs26 \cf2 \cb3 The stack is plural and unequal, matching the literature synthesis.
\f0 \'a0Geometry (H1) is the strongest and most principled layer \'97 it's\'a0
\f3\i derived
\f0\i0 \'a0(computational mechanics predicts the simplex before you look inside) rather than reverse-engineered, and the fractal belief geometry is visible in the linear readout. Circuits (H2) are real but form discontinuously. Activation-feature SAEs (H3/H4) are the weak joint: on known concepts they only achieve\'a0
\f1 parity
\f0 \'a0with a logistic probe, and lose slightly on the harder concept.\cb1 \

\f1 \cb3 Four findings that would have been false claims without controls:
\f0 \cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1 \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
E2 positional shortcut
\f0 \'a0\'97 the fixed-offset\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cb4 [x;x]
\f0\fs26 \cb3 \'a0design gave\'a0
\f3\i perfect
\f0\i0 \'a0in-context copying with\'a0
\f1 zero
\f0 \'a0induction attention. A behavioral metric certified a capability the mechanism didn't implement. Randomizing the gap made the induction head appear. This is the Jonas\'96Kording failure mode, reproduced accidentally on a system whose ground truth we knew.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
E4 non-determinism
\f0 \'a0\'97 identical runs gave SAE accuracy 0.786 / 0.843 / 0.857. Root cause: the memory-efficient attention kernel's backward pass.\'a0
\f1 7 points of drift is larger than the effects being claimed.
\f0 \'a0Fixed by pinning the math SDP backend +\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cb4 CUBLAS_WORKSPACE_CONFIG
\f0\fs26 \cb3 ; now bit-reproducible.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
E4 criterion drift
\f0 \'a0\'97 the code enforced\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cb4 raw \uc0\u8805  sae \u8722  1pt
\f0\fs26 \cb3 , but SPEC.md preregistered "SAE beats raw by >5pts consistently". The code had silently drifted to a\'a0
\f3\i stricter bar than was registered
\f0\i0 . Restored to the registered rule.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
E5 tautological metric
\f0 \'a0\'97 the headline "4.8\'d7 smaller circuit" is\'a0
\f1 0.2086 \uc0\u8776  the imposed q=0.20
\f0 . AbsTopK keeps exactly 20% of weights by construction, and both models kept the same 6 nodes, so the ratio reports\'a0
\f3\i our hyperparameter
\f0\i0 , not learned structure.\'a0
\f1 Zero variance across seeds was the tell
\f0 \'a0\'97 a perfectly reproducible result can be reproducing a constant.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 Plus: two tests were overwriting real\'a0
\f2\fs24 \cb4 results/
\f0\fs26 \cb3 \'a0artifacts with toy-config output, which is how VALIDATION.md briefly quoted numbers no real run produced. Fixed, with an AST-based guard test.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1 \cf2 \cb3 H3's refutation is honest but domain-limited
\f0 : on a 3-symbol synthetic process, an\'a0
\f3\i untrained
\f0\i0 \'a0net's activations are low-dimensional and trivially reconstructable, so the random model gets the\'a0
\f3\i lower
\f0\i0 \'a0FVU. The separation runs opposite to "trained models are more structured" \'97 the metric is scoring reconstructability, not features.\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

